<title>UK: Bad weather shuts Russia's Novorossiisk oil port.</title>
<headline>Bad weather shuts Russia's Novorossiisk oil port.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's main oil export terminal at Novorossiisk on the Black Sea closed early on Friday due to high winds and swell, a shipping source said.</p>
<p>The port shut at 0630 local time, leaving six crude tankers waiting at anchor, the source added.</p>
<p>A small fuel oil vessel was alongside berth number three but had not started to take on product.</p>
<p>Novorossiisk reopened early Thursday after an 18-hour shutdown.</p>
<p>Other oil ports on the Black Sea and Baltic were open and operating normally, shipping sources said.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7930</p>
